============================================================
       COLLEGE MANAGEMENT SYSTEM (CMS) - LEARNING GUIDE
============================================================
Version: 1.0 (Mobile PWA & AI Integrated)
Audience: Students, Faculty, and Administrators
Format: Professional Training Manual

------------------------------------------------------------
1. INTRODUCTION
------------------------------------------------------------
Welcome to the next generation of College Management. This 
system is a high-performance web platform built with 
Next.js 16 and Supabase, designed to streamline academic 
workflows through AI, Automation, and Mobile accessibility.

------------------------------------------------------------
2. STUDENT LEARNING PATH
------------------------------------------------------------
A. THE AI TUTOR (Killer Feature)
1. Go to the main Dashboard.
2. Click "Upload Syllabus" in the AI Tutor card.
3. Select any PDF (less than 5MB).
4. Type questions like "Summarize Chapter 1" or "Help me 
   prepare for the midterm."
5. The AI (Google Gemini) will analyze your specific file 
   and provide custom guidance.

B. ASSIGNMENTS & SUBMISSIONS
1. Navigate to the "Assignments" tab.
2. View active tasks and deadlines.
3. Upload your work (PDF/DOCX/JPG).
4. Once graded by a teacher, you will receive an automatic
   email notification via the Resend API.

C. FINANCE & FEES
1. Check your "Fees Status" on the dashboard.
2. View detailed breakdowns of pending and paid amounts.
3. Download payment receipts directly from the portal.

------------------------------------------------------------
3. TEACHER / FACULTY MASTERY
------------------------------------------------------------
A. PORTAL ACCESS
- Teachers have a dedicated "Faculty Portal" within the 
  Dashboard.
- Use the "Quick Demo Sheet" in the sidebar for login 
  testing (teacher@college.edu / teacher123).

B. GRADING WORKFLOW
1. Select an assignment to review.
2. Open student submissions (PDF/IMG).
3. Assign a numeric grade and add feedback.
4. Click "Submit Grade". The system handles the database 
   update and student email notification simultaneously.

------------------------------------------------------------
4. ADMINISTRATOR & SYSTEM CONTROL
------------------------------------------------------------
A. INSTITUTION BRANDING
1. Log in as Super Admin (admin@college.edu / admin123).
2. Go to "Settings".
3. Upload your College Logo (transparent PNG recommended).
4. Update the "Institution Name". This will change the 
   branding across the sidebar and every report page.

B. SYSTEM MODES (DEMO VS LIVE)
- Toggle "Live Mode" on when the institution is ready for 
  official use. This hides all demo badges and credential 
  sheets.

C. THE DANGER ZONE (SYSTEM WIPE)
- Located at the bottom of Settings.
- Use "Clean Software" to wipe all attendance, assignment, 
  and fee data while preserving the Admin accounts.
- CAUTION: This action is irreversible. Always back up the 
  database first.

------------------------------------------------------------
5. MOBILE APP (PWA) INSTALLATION
------------------------------------------------------------
- Open the CMS URL on your phone.
- iOS: Tap "Share" -> "Add to Home Screen".
- Android: Tap the three dots (menu) -> "Install App".
- The system will now behave as a native mobile application 
  with its own icon and offline capabilities.

------------------------------------------------------------
6. TECHNICAL STACK (DEVELOPER NOTES)
------------------------------------------------------------
- Framework: Next.js 16 (App Router + Turbopack)
- Database: Supabase (Auth, DB, Storage)
- Emails: Resend API
- AI: Google Generative AI (Gemini 1.5)
- Deployment: Vercel (Production)

